<p>President Trump said he may withdraw the United States from NATO after criticizing European allies for refusing to send ships to help unblock the Strait of Hormuz near Iran, deepening a transatlantic dispute already sharpened by the Middle East war. The remarks, published and reported on April 1, revived a long-running question: can a U.S. president take the country out of the alliance without Congress? Multiple reports say the answer remains legally contested. The immediate stakes are twofold. First, the comments add to uncertainty around NATO’s future at a moment of wider security strain. Second, they test a 2023 U.S. law meant to block a unilateral withdrawal by requiring congressional approval or Senate consent. Even so, there is a stabilizing factor: NATO’s treaty framework, allied institutions, and U.S. domestic checks mean any break would face political and legal resistance rather than happen overnight.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/0aiGzvutfNKzpQVemwLyektgyc6rTFCYq8cPVAucZIPanshz76nGopVULcsPoEPQw7gBcPADQ_3rsDpj6EmBsNMLjesgR21lB_61mkqdYsHhfymi25MLGhsUy66gJbrw54HqwTrRrGUrQY6b-tA7X8glBqT7BG2fgAJXMuI2JxFzkRsBM1tJwYLlrDRpaTehg_tUT5ZM1fMPsPuBI45Ks9XxkqpA0RX58j3mGiA' alt='President Trump during a meeting linked to the widening dispute with NATO allies.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Legal hurdle: Congress added language to the annual defense bill in 2023 barring a president from suspending, terminating, or withdrawing from NATO without either two-thirds Senate approval or an act of Congress.</li><li>Treaty process: Article 13 of the North Atlantic Treaty says a member can leave one year after giving notice of denunciation to the United States government. That clause is now central to the legal debate because Washington itself is the treaty depositary.</li><li>Alliance age: NATO was founded in 1949 and now links North America and Europe through a collective-defense pact that has survived repeated internal disputes, including earlier strains during President Trump’s first term.</li><li>Iran linkage: The latest dispute stems from President Trump’s complaint that allies were not backing U.S. goals on Iran and had declined to contribute naval support around the Strait of Hormuz.</li></ul><blockquote>They don&#x27;t support us. Why should we support them? - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: He tied his threat to burden-sharing inside the alliance and to support for U.S. policy on Iran, arguing that allies were not backing Washington when asked to help in the Strait of Hormuz. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c79je4vldq5o'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>U.S. Congress: Lawmakers from both parties previously moved to limit any unilateral NATO exit by writing explicit restrictions into law, signaling broad institutional support for preserving the alliance. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-withdraw-nato-require-congress-approval/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>European allies: Several allies have resisted being drawn more deeply into the U.S. confrontation with Iran. That stance helped fuel the latest rupture, but it also reflects concern about widening the conflict. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/trump-lashes-out-at-nato-allies-over-unpopular-mideast-war-widening-transatlantic-rift'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Legal experts: Experts cited in the coverage say it is unclear whether courts would uphold a unilateral withdrawal attempt, because the Constitution does not explicitly spell out how the United States leaves treaties. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/explainer-can-trump-pull-us-out-nato'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/explainer-can-trump-pull-the-us-out-of-nato'>Explainer: Can Trump pull the US out of NATO?</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c79je4vldq5o'>What do Trump&#x27;s latest comments on leaving Nato mean for the alliance?</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/is-nato-becoming-collateral-damage-in-president-donald-trumps-us-iran-war-middle-east-conflict-11300111#publisher=newsstand'>Is NATO Becoming Collateral Damage In Trump&#x27;s Iran War?</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-withdraw-nato-require-congress-approval/'>Trump says he may withdraw U.S. from NATO. The law says he can&#x27;t without Congress.</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/explainer-can-trump-pull-us-out-nato'>Explainer-Can Trump pull the US out of NATO?</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/trump-lashes-out-at-nato-allies-over-unpopular-mideast-war-widening-transatlantic-rift'>Trump lashes out at NATO allies over unpopular Mideast war, widening transatlantic rift</a> - pbs.org</li></ul>